{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark hark good traveler bound for Nippon’s fair shores\nLet quill and ink weave thee a journey grand\nThy days shall dance with samurai and gods and flowers\nA tale most noble in this land enchanted\n\nUpon the morn of thy first day do rise with zeal\nTo Tokyo’s heart where neon lights do gleam\nAscend the tower where the sun doth kiss thy face\nThen wander through the streets where old and new do meet\nIn Shinjuku’s pulse where lanterns flicker soft and low\nAnd Akihabara’s glow doth call thee to its circuit bright\nAt eve do feast on sushi fresh as morning dew\nAnd sake that flows like rivers through thy veins\n\nOn the morrow let thy feet bear thee to Asakusa’s shrine\nWhere temple bells do chime in rhythms old and wise\nThrough Sumida’s waters glide upon a boat so fair\nPast bridges red where cherry blossoms sway and sigh\nAt dusk do traverse streets where maidens in kimono tread\nAnd buy the sweets that crunch like autumn’s crisp embrace\n\nLo the third day calls thee to Nikko’s sacred wood\nWhere shrines stand tall ‘neath heavens golden gaze\nThrough waterfalls that roar like thunder’s ancient tongue\nAnd halls that whisper tales of emperors long past\nAbide in onsen where the earth doth warm thy bones\nAnd let the steam erase the dust of mortal care\n\nNow forth to Hakone where the mountain looms so high\nAnd views unfold like paintings in a master’s hand\nAmong the clouds where Fuji’s peak doth touch the sky\nAnd geysers hiss like dragons waking from their sleep\nDo bathe in waters said to grant thee youthful grace\nThen dine on black eggs that taste of earth and time\n\nUpon the fourth dawn let trains thy swift steed carry\nTo Kyoto’s halls where history doth breathe and sigh\nThrough golden pavilions where the koi do dart and play\nAnd gardens where the moss grows soft as whispered prayers\nAt Fushimi’s slope where barrels line the misty air\nDo taste the wine that turns to silk upon thy tongue\n\nThe fifth day gifts thee to Nara’s ancient grace\nWhere deer do bow with eyes so kind and old\nThrough Todai’s doors where Buddha’s gaze doth hold thee fast\nAnd lanterns float like fireflies upon the river’s face\nThen wander paths where monks in robes of deepest hue\nDo chant the names of gods in tones both soft and deep\n\nOn the sixth do rise and seek the coast’s embrace\nWhere Hiroshima’s peace doth shine like morning’s first light\nAt Miyajima’s tide where torii stands half-drowned in sea\nAnd its waters call thee to a dance so wild and free\nThen feast on okonomiyaki’s warmth and savory might\nAs stars above begin to pierce the velvet night\n\nNow lo the seventh day thy final in this realm so fair\nTo Osaka’s joy where laughter rings like bells at prayer\nThrough Dotonbori’s streets where signs do flash and gleam\nAnd takoyaki’s bubbles pop like fireworks in dream\nAt Universal’s gates where heroes walk and fight\nDo laugh with children who still dream the world is bright\n\nThus ends thy journey through this isle so sweet and dire\nWhere every step a story every glance a rhyme\nWith heart full rich and soul both worn and brightened still\nReturn thou home a poet in this land divine.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " h", "logprob": -1.5492585897445679}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0038220465648919344}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -0.4081418216228485}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.351406067609787}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0007333449902944267}, {"token": " bound", "logprob": -2.3361754417419434}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.01646420732140541}, {"token": " Nippon", "logprob": -1.569198489189148}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.48478806018829346}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.4478911757469177}, {"token": " shores", "logprob": -1.8614699840545654}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.08